            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The `sa` is a surrounding operator that takes a target to operate upon (i.e. for which to add surrounding parts to the left and right). The `iw` and `w` are two different targets that select different parts of text: `iw` is \"inside word\" textobject (selects the widest contiguous keyword or non-keyword characters at cursor) while `w` is a \"word\" movement (select from the cursor to the start of the next word). You can see how they work by starting a visual mode with `v` and typing each of the three.\n\nSo \"If my cursor is on the first letter of the word, the `w` and `iw` behavior should be identical\" is not an expectation that is aligned with how Neovim works. And as a consequence, surrounding operator also works as expected here.\n\n",
