            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> For what it's worth, kylechui's [nvim-surround](https://github.com/kylechui/nvim-surround) plugin work as I described, which I think makes more sense.\n\nYes, it appears so. As is 'tpope/vim-surround'. Both of them handle add a special logic to ignore trailing (but not leading) whitespace in a target region. I.e. even `ysaw)` would still ignore trailing whitespace. This is not a universally agreed good thing either (tpope/vim-surround#138).\n\nBut this still doesn't make more sense as this deviates from what built-in operators do. For example, `yw` will include trailing whitesapce. And so has to every other custom operator.",
